oracle.summary:
The independent CDR-012 expectations are built under /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-Investment-System1/33fa0ec1-e143-560f-87b9-563dee3b3dc5/scratchpad/wf11/prep-cdr012-oracle/base/, which is a byte-identical copy of the wf9 CDR-010 oracle plus new cdr012 files.

The CDR-012 reference is the CDR-010 default plus one rule: deg == B gives class NOT_RUN. It exists in a primary version and an exact-rational ALT version, and the two are bit-identical on 752/752 cases.

expected_cdr012.json (sha256 d98fae60…) has 752 cases: 710 STAT graded bit-exact over 71,899 replicates, 37 F3 NOT_RUN, and 5 ungraded UNDEFINED_SE. Re-grading the 681-case battery made 0 cases NOT_RUN and changed 0 other values. The dedicated fixtures are:
- 37 all-degenerate cases across B 1..199 (positive, negative and zero mean, B=1, constant blocks, rounding-induced, seed-lucky B19, subnormal);
- 17 boundary cases with deg == B-1;
- 16 F1 detectors: 12 E-SQUARE plus 4 refuter cases. The refuter p-flips were verified: .15 vs .20 and .10 vs .15;
- 14 near-undefined cases that keep a p.

compare_cdr012.py treats NOT_RUN as an outcome class and has a configurable, documented NOT_RUN adapter mapping (exception MRO, reason regex, result keys, p None). Against v2 at e0b6d80 it catches F1 on 16/16 detectors (31 rows) and F3 on 37/37, with zero false mismatches on the boundary and near-undefined cases. Its mismatch rows equal the oracle's pow+F3-off mutant row for row. All 12 mutants are caught.

The registry probe at e0b6d80 reproduces GIE-010 F3 at registry level: STAT_PASS with 8/8 all-degenerate cells REJECT_H0 (S1), and STAT_PASS with the single F3 cell REJECT_H0 (S2). The S3 near-undefined control stays STAT_PASS, as CDR-012 expects. In-memory shim self-tests confirm the probe passes a compliant F3 implementation and fails an epsilon guard.

The README gives the exact commands for the new head and the SHA256SUMS covers 90 files. Remote refs were unchanged throughout, and the private clone and extracts are deleted. The only blocker is OWNER_ACTION: Codex still has to reach CDR-012 HANDOFF_READY on #31.
